[mcmahan@cs.unca.edu (Scott McMahan) writes:]
[] MY QUESTION now centers on:  has anyone ever completed the game without
[] using the X exploration mode?  I don't think it's possible ...

the purpose of explore-mode is to enable the player to get game
insights.  you are then supposed to play a normal game and hopefully
eventually win.  many, i believe, have done this ...

[] even if you begin with a wand of wishes -- I wished for the 
[] "blessed scroll of recharging" and all it gave me was one wish more :-)
[] I always think a wand of death is a good thing to wish for...

please take this constructively ...

worrying about getting more wishes in explore-mode is kinda pointless.
you should focus on a specific feature and then wish your way around
that point until you get the hang of it.

also your strategy of wishing for a wand of death lacks subtlety and
is inappropriate in most cases.  answer the question: "what happens
after the charges are gone?" and you begin to get an idea of why this
tact is short-sighted, typically.

you are right on one point: survival is the key (brilliant -dave-!).
generally you want to make incremental adjustments in your status to
increase your odds of survival in the current environment and you
basically assume that you can sustain yourself in this environment,
perhaps indefinitely, and that you'll explore at just the right pace
so that things don't get out of hand.

